Layer A ("Sanskrit Library TEI/XML edition") turns out not to be a
downloadable file: it's served through an undocumented JSON endpoint
behind the reader page's JavaScript (LoadText?text=fgveda_prAtiSAKya),
found by reading sl.js/sl.model.js rather than any published API. One
inspection fetch (318 KB, 1,067 sūtras, SLP1, with a cross-reference
apparatus and a "Version 0.1" label) confirmed paṭala 10 = 22 sūtras and
paṭala 11 = 71 sūtras exactly, and verified several sūtras word-for-word
against text that had appeared unattributed in the original Gemini-
derived review — including the catuḥkrama sūtra, now precisely citable
as RVPr_11.19. Adds the verified-sample table, the real per-paṭala
sūtra counts, a populated rule-database example, and an access-ethics
note: a full 1,067-sūtra bulk pull through the same undocumented
endpoint needs an explicit go-ahead, separate from the one-off
inspection already done here.

